  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">China Partnering Award: Imperial College London - China collaboration on Actinobacillus pleuropneumoniae vaccines, diagnostics, and pathogenesis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The bacterium Actinobacillus pleuropneumonaie (APP) causes lung disease in pigs and is responsible for is responsible for mortality and economic losses in China. This project will work with Chinese partners to focus on vaccine development, diagnostics, population biology and understanding the basic pathogenicity mechanisms of APP.</narrative>
  </description>
